    zero under the other prefix - it is the same javax API republished under a
    different artifactId - and its class set is IDENTICAL to the javax-named
    2.2.1 artifact. Carrying both would place 211 duplicate javax/persistence
    classes on the classpath under order-sensitive, non-reproducible
    resolution. The javax-named 2.2.1 artifact adds exactly two annotation
    container types over 2.1.0, and NEITHER appears anywhere in the source, so
    the advance carries ZERO source impact and ZERO effect on the schema
    generated from the persistence mappings.
    Scale for context: main source carries 1610 occurrences of the persistence
    package and 69 of its criteria subpackage, every one of them left
    untouched. Under R-T1 the javax strings in this file are CORRECT and must
    be preserved verbatim - they must never be rewritten.
